    {
      "id": "claim_1532fef088cb474b83fd465d912c35a2",
      "statement": "The consentsGate rule's check compares the full condition string and status_code 451 rather than just the rule's presence, so a version bump is reported as outstanding work; its apply sets on_error: 'allow' so a rule that cannot be evaluated cannot lock everyone out, and /users/me is deliberately not excluded so the client learns of the gate by the first blocked read.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L282-L317",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61bb3204eef5b835755b0b6f6ddeb8cd77fc51636fd8e642903f24bd6671900f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ad224bc4edf3477aa3d34310dda26ae2",
      "statement": "The consents gate setup's ordered step list is the reused accounts steps minus appPointsAtService, then user schema storage with a canonical compare, /users _meta jsonSchema attachment, the userCanPatchOwnConsents permission with mergeRequest and bson-request-whitelist(consents), the account-properties-claims addition, guards feature installation, and the consentsGate rule with 451 and on_error allow — after which appPointsAtService is re-appended last.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L183-L321",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:619a44c193eecb68e8113d1acfb71201467f521093d28546b07ca2231c2203af:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_55b8ed97f46842f0b61d2b1439b04f40",
      "statement": "The consentsGate condition blocks when either acceptance is missing — not (tos-match and pp-match), never not-tos and not-pp, which would block only users who accepted neither.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L119-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a66f4211e0c82561689273f6a9948cad26397bc3a226fd957eae0081f17bdd2e:"
