        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_235e8a8d731f41c6adfa46eb24945c19",
      "statement": "The users collection validation step attaches the schema by PATCH-ing /users with { jsonSchema: { schemaId } }, but reads the attachment back from the collection's own properties at /users/_meta; reading /users itself never shows jsonSchema.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L204-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3489aa0d533e0d0c0c8706b749aa63c0a0dc7b368ed88dc80dd90e416714f49:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3397f82f2858454b8be2d7a62e62d9b8",
      "statement": "userCanPatchOwnConsents permits only the user role to PATCH its own consents field (path-template, method, @user._id or @user.sub match, bson-request-whitelist(consents)); its mergeRequest writes latestConsents as a nested object to avoid MongoDB ConflictingUpdateOperators and _$pushes onto the consents history so acceptances accumulate rather than overwrite.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L220-L248",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d691885900551d601f5fe1163ab4cf3a3794f941d8ea4050d1ed2ae1e06c83e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c79ebdf8262d46d8bdb1475f8d63be19",
      "statement": "latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp are added to the auth feature's account-properties-claims by set-union because the guard reads the token rather than the database; a missing claim compares false for every token-authenticated user, including those who just accepted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
